FINDINGS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
F1 (CLOSED — my attempt-1 finding). The three dashboard wiring points that
   survived every attempt-1 mutation are now each guarded by their own
   real-HTTP test: B_dash, B_kpis and B_chart each fail exactly one test and
   leave the other two passing. This finding is discharged.
F2 (backlog, PRE-EXISTING, master-native, out of scope per ruling d).
   CombinedCumulativeBalance's walk assumes per-month |sum| partitions
   range-level |sum|, which is false whenever any single month is
   refund-dominant. My PROBE-MM shows the invariant breaking with
   planExclusions=nil, i.e. on master's own code path, so SY4 neither causes
   nor worsens it — but it is a real correctness bug in a rendered chart
   (the cumulative trace), reachable from ordinary data given the ledger's
   "type is INFERRED, not bank-supplied" convention: one misclassified
   large credit is enough. Worth its own task; note the worker deliberately
   omitted a walk test for the remainder fixture for exactly this reason,
   which is the right call under the ruling but leaves the bug unrecorded
   in code. Recommend a skipped/documented test or an issue so it is not
   rediscovered a fourth time.
F3 (commit hygiene, unchanged, not SY4's): untracked 16MB ELF
   `budget2.old-1345` in the repo root, not gitignored — a blind
   `git add -A` would commit it. Not executed.

